[Term]
id: HMDM:0000240
name: NADH oxidase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "NADH oxidase (NOX) is a member of the flavoprotein disulfide reductase family that catalyses the pyridine-nucleotide-dependent reduction of various substrates, including O2, H2O2 and thioredoxin. NADH oxidases (NOXs) catalysing the oxidation of NADH to yield NAD+ and H2O, H2O2, or both play an important role in protecting organisms from oxidative stress and maintaining the balance of NAD+/NADH." [PMID:10629192, PMID:27737924]
is_a: HMDM:0000264 ! Flavoenzymes
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000261
name: anti-parkinson agent
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Parkinson’s disease (PD) is characterized by prodromal symptoms, motor difficulties, and psychological or cognitive problems. As a progressive neurodegenerative disease, PD causes focal degeneration of midbrain dopamine (MesDA) neurons. Antiparkinson agents are agents used for treatment of Parkinson’s disease. Medications, include dopamine agonists, monoamine oxidase B inhibitors, levodopa plus carbidopa, etc., anticholinergics and amantadine. Also, new theraputic approaches include, based on recent advances in the understanding of the pathophysiology of Parkinson’s disease, genetic and disease-modifying approaches to reduce abnormal accumulation and aggregation of alpha-synuclein (aSYN), mitochondrial dysfunction, and dysfunction of lysosomal proteins, as well as approaches to reduce neuroinflammation and increase neurorestoration." [PMID:30661251, PMID:35601911]
is_a: HMDM:0000073 ! drug class
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000264
name: Flavoenzymes
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Flavoenzymes are redox proteins that catalyze a wide diversity of biological reactions ranging from O2 activation, to aromatic hydroxylations, dehydrogenations, and reactions in which they can accept or donate one or two electrons." [PMID:10494549]
is_a: HMDM:0000012 ! gene family
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000265
name: FMN-dependent NADH azoreductase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Azoreductases reduce the azo bond (N=N) in azo dyes to produce colorless amine products. FMN-dependent NADH azoreductase are flavin-dependent, specifically flavin mononucleotide (FMN) enzymes, that are able to reductively cleave compounds containing an azo bond and where NADH is used as an electron donor for the reduction of substrates by azoreductases." [PMID:18791262, PMID:27487252]
is_a: HMDM:0000264 ! Flavoenzymes
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000266
name: FMN-dependent NAD(P)H nitroreductase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "The FMN-dependent NAD(P)H nitroreductase catalyze the sequential reduction of nitro groups through the addition of electron pairs from NAD(P)H and flavin mononucleotide (FMN) ." []
is_a: HMDM:0000264 ! Flavoenzymes
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000269
name: FMN-dependent Nitroreductase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Nitroreductases are a family of evolutionarily related proteins involved in reducing nitroaromatic and nitroheterocyclic compounds. FMN-dependent Nitroreductase uses flavin mononucleotide (FMN) as the cofactor in this reaction. FMN usually works as a prosthetic groups in flavoproteins to which they are tightly bound. Flavodoxins are small monomeric flavoproteins (15–22 kDa) that noncovalently bind a single FMN molecule, acting as a redox center. The flavodoxin scaffold contributes to the mechanism of electron transfer by stabilizing the FMN molecule in an environment that promotes the highly negative redox potential required for its biochemical activity." [PMID:15184374, PMID:34613761]
is_a: HMDM:0000264 ! Flavoenzymes
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000270
name: FMN-dependent NADPH nitroreductase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Oxygen-insensitive nitroreductases are a group of flavoenzymes, belonging to oxido-reductases, that are able to reduce nitro compounds depending on nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide availability (NAD(P)H). Nitroreductases were separated of others reductases due to their capacity to reduce nitro compounds. FMN-dependent NADPH nitroreductase uses flavin mononucleotide (FMN) as the cofactor and NADPH as a reducing equivalent." [PMID:28545445, PMID:34613761]
is_a: HMDM:0000264 ! Flavoenzymes
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000271
name: Acyltransferase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Acyltransferase or transacylase utilize these activated acyl chains and transfer them to a variety of different substrates or polymerize them." []
is_a: HMDM:0000012 ! gene family
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000272
name: Arylamine N-acetyltransferases (NATs)
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Arylamine N-acetyltransferases (NATs) are polymorphic drug-metabolizing enzymes, acetylating arylamine carcinogens and drugs including hydralazine and sulphonamides." []
is_a: HMDM:0000271 ! Acyltransferase
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000274
name: sulfatase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Sulfatases, which cleave sulfate esters in biological systems, play a key role in regulating the sulfation states that determine the function of many physiological molecules." [PMID:15493058]
is_a: HMDM:0000012 ! gene family
is_a: HMDM:0000900 ! Drug activation enzyme
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000279
name: Arylsulfatase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Arylsulfatases are enzymes which catalyze the hydrolysis of arylsulfate ester bonds to release a free sulfonate." [PMID:27654655]
is_a: HMDM:0000274 ! sulfatase
