is_a: HMDM:0000073 ! drug class
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000792
name: HAD superfamily
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "The haloacid dehydrogenase (HAD) superfamily includes phosphatases, phosphonatases, P-type ATPases, beta-phosphoglucomutases, phosphomannomutases, and dehalogenases, which are involved in detoxification." [PMID:7966317]
is_a: HMDM:0000012 ! gene family
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000793
name: AcbK
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "A self-resistance mechanism is encoded within the biosynthetic gene cluster (BGC) for acarbose (acb) production; a specific kinase, AcbK, phosphorylates acarbose at the O6A hydroxyl and renders it inactive." [PMID:11937512, PMID:34819672]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
is_a: HMDM:0000820 ! pfkB family carbohydrate kinase
relationship: RO:0000056 HMDM:0000495 ! participates in phosphorylation of a molecule
relationship: RO:0002447 CHEBI:2376 ! phosphorylates acarbose
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
id: HMDM:0000820
name: pfkB family carbohydrate kinase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "The pfkB family of enzymes across kingdoms includes ribokinases, phosphofructokinases, adenosine kinases (ADKs) and several others with diverse substrate specificities. Typical PfkB protein structure is a large domain consisting of a beta-sheet sandwiched between several alpha-helices, and a smaller domain, known as the lid domain, comprised of another beta-sheet attached to the larger domain by short loops that act as a hinge. Binding of substrates to pfkB proteins follows ordered bi-bi kinetics where the carbohydrate enters first, followed by ATP. PfkB proteins possess two signature motifs: a di-gly (GG) motif in the N-terminal region and a G/AXGD motif in the C-terminal region. The role of each motif has been identified through mutational and structural analyses. The GG motif provides flexibility in the hinge region that connects the lid and the large domain. The aspartate in the G/AXGD motif acts as a base during catalysis and activates the C6 fructose hydroxyl group for nucleophilic attack on the gamma-phosphate in ATP. Many pfkB proteins are active as dimers generated through interactions between the lid domains of two monomers. Aside from their regulation by ATP, pfkB family enzymes are activated by both monovalent and divalent cationic cofactors." [PMID:28441933]
is_a: HMDM:0000012 ! gene family
is_a: HMDM:0000901 ! Drug self-resistant enzyme
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280

[Term]
