[Term]
id: HMDM:0000825
name: Cyclomaltodextrinase
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "Cyclomaltodextrinase (CDase) is a maltogenic amylase and neopullulanase are reported to be capable of hydrolyzing all or two of the following three types of substrates: cyclomaltodextrins (CDs); pullulan; and starch." [PMID:10825529, PMID:29392561]
