[Term]
id: HMDM:0000902
name: apg
namespace: human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology
def: "The apg is an acarbose-preferred glucosidase that was discovered in intestinal bacteria from patients with Type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) chronic metabolic disease. The Apg hydrolyses acarbose into small molecules (acarviosine-glucose and acarviosine) with loss of inhibitor function to porcine pancreatic amylase and is widely distributed in human intestinal microorganisms, especially in Klebsiella." [PMID:37157031]
